  "details": "It's difficult to draw accurately in desktop mode when holding a QvPen in hand while holding the Tab key, because the cursor position on UI does not match the QvPen tip position used to draw.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Launch VRChat in desktop mode (windowed). ([Avatar Testing Chamber](https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_a5e9ec13-36b1-4e63-ae0c-dab9023401f9/info) by Ziggor)\n\n2. Print something, or go near UI button elements in world.\n\n3. Hold down the Tab key and try to highlight the print or UI elements. The selection of UI elements should match your actual mouse cursor position.\n\n4. Grab a QvPen from the world.\n\n5. Try drawing with a QvPen while holding the Tab key. Notice the position where QvPen is drawing, and where your mouse cursor actually is.\n\nSee the attached video.\n\nExpected result: The QvPen tip for drawing should match the actual mouse cursor position.\n\nActual result: The QvPen tip for drawing does not match the actual cursor position, the VRChat / OS cursor moves faster than the QvPen tip.\n\nI would test in Build `1867` which felt comfortable, but the `minSupportedClientBuildNumber` is currently `1902`. Build `1902` is also experiencing this issue.",
